1
00:00:00,342 --> 00:00:02,636
Last video ended here, with this density.

2
00:00:03,501 --> 00:00:05,267
Where is X most likely to be,

3
00:00:05,830 --> 00:00:08,418
and where's the middle, with half the probability

4
00:00:08,459 --> 00:00:09,060
on each side?

5
00:00:09,924 --> 00:00:12,415
For this symmetric hump, both answers are one,

6
00:00:12,818 --> 00:00:13,621
right in the centre.

7
00:00:14,405 --> 00:00:17,357
Now a cookie, four centimetres in radius, with

8
00:00:17,398 --> 00:00:18,984
its choc chips spread evenly.

9
00:00:19,648 --> 00:00:21,633
In the ideal model, a chip lands at

10
00:00:21,674 --> 00:00:23,217
a random point on the cookie.

11
00:00:23,881 --> 00:00:25,657
Let X be its distance from the centre.

12
00:00:26,343 --> 00:00:29,096
Its density is x over eight, from zero

13
00:00:29,218 --> 00:00:29,619
to four.

14
00:00:30,404 --> 00:00:32,129
It climbs the whole way, because the outer

15
00:00:32,170 --> 00:00:33,233
rings hold more cookie.

16
00:00:33,855 --> 00:00:35,782
So distances near the edge are the most

17
00:00:35,883 --> 00:00:38,051
likely, and the density peaks at four.

18
00:00:38,915 --> 00:00:41,825
Yet half the probability lies within about two

19
00:00:41,886 --> 00:00:43,993
point eight three centimetres of the centre.

20
00:00:44,898 --> 00:00:47,243
So the most likely value and the middle

21
00:00:47,625 --> 00:00:48,647
can be far apart.

22
00:00:49,330 --> 00:00:50,436
How do we find each one?

23
00:00:51,088 --> 00:00:53,121
The mode is the value where the density

24
00:00:53,283 --> 00:00:53,825
is highest.

25
00:00:54,691 --> 00:00:56,576
Here's why X is most likely to be

26
00:00:56,617 --> 00:00:57,499
found near there.

27
00:00:58,383 --> 00:01:01,691
Slide a narrow window, two tenths wide, along

28
00:01:01,712 --> 00:01:02,092
the hump.

29
00:01:02,755 --> 00:01:04,722
It catches the most area, and so the

30
00:01:04,764 --> 00:01:07,474
most probability, near the top of this symmetric

31
00:01:07,535 --> 00:01:07,755
hump.

32
00:01:08,599 --> 00:01:11,106
Near one, it catches about zero point one

33
00:01:11,187 --> 00:01:11,547
five,

34
00:01:12,050 --> 00:01:14,516
and near zero point two, about zero point

35
00:01:14,578 --> 00:01:15,199
zero five.

36
00:01:15,842 --> 00:01:17,486
So the mode is at the peak of

37
00:01:17,808 --> 00:01:17,887
f,

38
00:01:18,611 --> 00:01:19,132
not of F.

39
00:01:20,316 --> 00:01:23,081
F only builds up probability, so its top

40
00:01:23,343 --> 00:01:24,965
doesn't tell you where f peaks.

41
00:01:25,608 --> 00:01:28,240
Finding the peak is a maximum problem, like

42
00:01:28,281 --> 00:01:29,285
the ones you've solved before.

43
00:01:30,049 --> 00:01:32,803
Write f as six x minus three x

44
00:01:32,864 --> 00:01:33,949
squared, over four.

45
00:01:34,693 --> 00:01:37,302
Its derivative is six minus six x, over

46
00:01:37,383 --> 00:01:40,052
four, which is zero at x equals one.

47
00:01:40,776 --> 00:01:43,508
The second derivative is minus three halves, which

48
00:01:43,549 --> 00:01:45,276
is negative, so that's a maximum.

49
00:01:46,100 --> 00:01:48,526
The mode is one, where the density is

50
00:01:48,748 --> 00:01:49,429
three quarters.

51
00:01:50,192 --> 00:01:52,615
And because this hump is symmetric about one,

52
00:01:53,137 --> 00:01:55,721
half the area lies on each side, so

53
00:01:55,742 --> 00:01:57,003
the median is one as well.

54
00:01:57,748 --> 00:01:59,723
F of one is a half, which checks

55
00:01:59,784 --> 00:01:59,844
it.

56
00:02:00,416 --> 00:02:03,191
But a density doesn't always have a stationary

57
00:02:03,252 --> 00:02:03,492
point.

58
00:02:04,096 --> 00:02:06,360
For the cookie, x over eight, from zero

59
00:02:06,381 --> 00:02:09,367
to four, the derivative is one eighth, and

60
00:02:09,408 --> 00:02:10,069
it's never zero.

61
00:02:10,892 --> 00:02:13,798
The density keeps climbing, so its greatest value

62
00:02:13,919 --> 00:02:15,983
is at the right-hand end, the edge of

63
00:02:16,004 --> 00:02:16,384
the cookie.

64
00:02:16,987 --> 00:02:18,080
The mode is four.

65
00:02:19,009 --> 00:02:21,581
So, just like any global maximum, check the

66
00:02:21,683 --> 00:02:22,626
endpoints as well.

67
00:02:23,532 --> 00:02:25,822
And if a density is completely flat,

68
00:02:26,325 --> 00:02:27,631
it has no single mode.

69
00:02:28,405 --> 00:02:29,196
Now the middle.

70
00:02:29,782 --> 00:02:32,194
The median, m, is the value with half

71
00:02:32,254 --> 00:02:33,460
the probability below it.

72
00:02:34,183 --> 00:02:36,831
That's an area on f, but F already

73
00:02:36,932 --> 00:02:37,774
holds the areas.

74
00:02:38,155 --> 00:02:40,163
So we solve F of m equals one

75
00:02:40,223 --> 00:02:40,464
half.

76
00:02:41,166 --> 00:02:42,887
For the cookie, F of x is the

77
00:02:42,967 --> 00:02:45,128
fraction of the cookie within x of the

78
00:02:45,188 --> 00:02:45,528
centre,

79
00:02:46,029 --> 00:02:48,610
pi x squared over pi times sixteen, which

80
00:02:48,690 --> 00:02:50,271
is x squared over sixteen.

81
00:02:50,873 --> 00:02:53,461
Integrating x over eight from zero gives the

82
00:02:53,503 --> 00:02:53,762
same.

83
00:02:54,305 --> 00:02:56,511
So m squared over sixteen is a half,

84
00:02:56,993 --> 00:02:59,199
m squared is eight, and m is two

85
00:02:59,260 --> 00:03:01,606
root two, about two point eight three.

86
00:03:02,268 --> 00:03:04,391
The negative root, minus two root two, is

87
00:03:04,553 --> 00:03:06,796
outside zero to four, so we reject it,

88
00:03:06,998 --> 00:03:07,498
and say so.

89
00:03:08,296 --> 00:03:11,031
The quartiles split the probability into quarters.

90
00:03:11,615 --> 00:03:14,665
The lower quartile solves F equals one quarter,

91
00:03:15,248 --> 00:03:17,755
and the upper quartile solves F equals three

92
00:03:17,816 --> 00:03:18,136
quarters.

93
00:03:18,819 --> 00:03:20,504
Here, the lower quartile is two,

94
00:03:21,107 --> 00:03:23,193
and the upper quartile is two root three,

95
00:03:23,676 --> 00:03:24,879
about three point four six.

96
00:03:25,765 --> 00:03:26,555
Now look at the cookie.

97
00:03:27,344 --> 00:03:29,831
Circles at two, two point eight three and

98
00:03:29,912 --> 00:03:32,339
three point four six cut it into four

99
00:03:32,400 --> 00:03:33,242
pieces of equal area.

100
00:03:34,548 --> 00:03:37,222
In this sample cookie, each holds fifteen of

101
00:03:37,263 --> 00:03:38,046
its sixty chips.

102
00:03:38,831 --> 00:03:40,316
A real cookie would only come close.

103
00:03:41,321 --> 00:03:43,786
The pieces get narrower towards the edge, because

104
00:03:43,828 --> 00:03:45,331
the density is higher there.

105
00:03:45,955 --> 00:03:48,289
A quarter of the probability fits into less

106
00:03:48,390 --> 00:03:48,611
width.

107
00:03:49,302 --> 00:03:50,230
One trap to avoid.

108
00:03:50,673 --> 00:03:52,823
The median comes from F, not f.

109
00:03:54,087 --> 00:03:56,330
Setting x over eight equal to a half

110
00:03:56,450 --> 00:03:58,473
gives four, which is just the end of

111
00:03:58,513 --> 00:03:59,014
the domain.

112
00:03:59,575 --> 00:04:01,518
The height of the density has nothing to

113
00:04:01,558 --> 00:04:02,640
do with half the area.

114
00:04:03,231 --> 00:04:03,839
Try one more.

115
00:04:04,467 --> 00:04:07,032
A density is three x squared over eight,

116
00:04:07,293 --> 00:04:08,194
from zero to two,

117
00:04:08,776 --> 00:04:11,080
and its F is x cubed over eight.

118
00:04:11,863 --> 00:04:14,288
The density keeps increasing, so the mode is

119
00:04:14,329 --> 00:04:15,351
at the end, at two.

120
00:04:16,114 --> 00:04:16,793
For the median,

121
00:04:17,295 --> 00:04:19,895
x cubed over eight equals a half, so

122
00:04:20,076 --> 00:04:22,316
x cubed is four, and m is the

123
00:04:22,357 --> 00:04:24,538
cube root of four, about one point five

124
00:04:24,559 --> 00:04:24,798
nine.

125
00:04:25,659 --> 00:04:27,924
In the same way, the lower quartile is

126
00:04:27,965 --> 00:04:29,908
the cube root of two, about one point

127
00:04:29,929 --> 00:04:30,289
two six.

128
00:04:31,173 --> 00:04:32,909
The median is well left of the mode.

129
00:04:33,494 --> 00:04:35,819
The density is low near zero, so it

130
00:04:35,860 --> 00:04:37,603
takes a lot of width there to collect

131
00:04:37,704 --> 00:04:38,585
half the probability.

132
00:04:39,188 --> 00:04:41,154
Here's why the difference matters in a real

133
00:04:41,215 --> 00:04:41,556
problem.

134
00:04:42,139 --> 00:04:43,420
A component's lifetime,

135
00:04:44,163 --> 00:04:48,030
L hours, has density three times four minus

136
00:04:48,352 --> 00:04:50,937
l, all squared, over sixty four, for l

137
00:04:51,038 --> 00:04:52,099
from zero to four.

138
00:04:53,062 --> 00:04:56,047
That density is highest at zero and falls

139
00:04:56,108 --> 00:04:58,813
the whole way, so the mode is zero.

140
00:04:59,756 --> 00:04:59,875
Its

141
00:05:00,437 --> 00:05:03,402
F is one minus four minus l, cubed,

142
00:05:03,824 --> 00:05:04,685
over sixty four.

143
00:05:05,629 --> 00:05:08,157
Setting F equal to a half gives four

144
00:05:08,198 --> 00:05:10,486
minus m, cubed, equals thirty two.

145
00:05:11,411 --> 00:05:13,557
So m is four minus the cube root

146
00:05:13,578 --> 00:05:14,320
of thirty two,

147
00:05:14,883 --> 00:05:16,728
about zero point eight three hours.

148
00:05:17,894 --> 00:05:20,262
Half of these components fail in under fifty

149
00:05:20,303 --> 00:05:22,651
minutes, even though some last up to four

150
00:05:22,692 --> 00:05:22,972
hours.

151
00:05:23,836 --> 00:05:26,141
The most likely lifetime and the median

152
00:05:26,643 --> 00:05:27,825
answer different questions.

153
00:05:28,556 --> 00:05:29,744
Here's a way to keep them apart.

154
00:05:30,529 --> 00:05:32,095
The mode is the top of f.

155
00:05:33,140 --> 00:05:35,643
The median and quartiles go across from F.

156
00:05:36,806 --> 00:05:38,649
For the median, go across from one half,

157
00:05:39,191 --> 00:05:40,272
and down to the axis.

158
00:05:42,987 --> 00:05:43,396
Your turn.

159
00:05:44,283 --> 00:05:47,512
A density is twelve x squared, times one

160
00:05:47,552 --> 00:05:50,059
minus x, for x from zero to one,

161
00:05:50,520 --> 00:05:51,503
and zero elsewhere.

162
00:05:52,185 --> 00:05:54,555
Find the mode, and justify your answer.

163
00:05:55,180 --> 00:05:55,992
Pause here to answer.

164
00:06:06,860 --> 00:06:09,662
Expand f, and its derivative is twenty four

165
00:06:09,902 --> 00:06:12,243
x minus thirty six x squared,

166
00:06:12,884 --> 00:06:15,646
or twelve x times two minus three x.

167
00:06:16,426 --> 00:06:19,182
That's zero at x equals zero, and at

168
00:06:19,263 --> 00:06:19,886
two thirds.

169
00:06:20,529 --> 00:06:22,554
But f of zero is zero, the lowest

170
00:06:22,594 --> 00:06:25,040
value, and f is zero at x equals

171
00:06:25,200 --> 00:06:25,661
one too.

172
00:06:26,545 --> 00:06:29,440
At two thirds, f is sixteen ninths, its

173
00:06:29,502 --> 00:06:30,164
greatest value.

174
00:06:30,689 --> 00:06:32,141
So the mode is two thirds.

175
00:06:32,971 --> 00:06:33,645
Zero is wrong.

176
00:06:33,889 --> 00:06:35,779
It's a stationary point, but a minimum.

177
00:06:37,373 --> 00:06:37,820
Last one.

178
00:06:38,528 --> 00:06:41,311
A continuous random variable has F of x

179
00:06:41,572 --> 00:06:44,355
equals x squared plus two x, all over

180
00:06:44,436 --> 00:06:44,615
eight,

181
00:06:45,157 --> 00:06:46,838
for x from zero to two.

182
00:06:47,841 --> 00:06:49,918
Find the lower quartile exactly.

183
00:06:50,687 --> 00:06:51,681
Pause here to answer.

184
00:07:02,296 --> 00:07:04,453
Solve F of x equals one quarter.

185
00:07:05,278 --> 00:07:07,365
So x squared plus two x equals two.

186
00:07:08,149 --> 00:07:08,849
Complete the square:

187
00:07:09,612 --> 00:07:12,055
x plus one, all squared, is three, so

188
00:07:12,297 --> 00:07:14,621
x is minus one, plus or minus root

189
00:07:14,662 --> 00:07:14,921
three.

190
00:07:16,105 --> 00:07:18,691
Minus one minus root three is outside zero

191
00:07:18,712 --> 00:07:19,894
to two, so reject it.

192
00:07:20,517 --> 00:07:22,922
The lower quartile is root three minus one,

193
00:07:23,385 --> 00:07:25,008
about zero point seven three.

194
00:07:25,892 --> 00:07:27,528
Keeping both roots is wrong.

195
00:07:27,974 --> 00:07:29,288
Only one is in the domain.

196
00:07:31,055 --> 00:07:33,499
So the mode is the peak of f,

197
00:07:33,921 --> 00:07:36,105
and the median and quartiles come from F.

198
00:07:37,731 --> 00:07:38,770
Next, a new question.

199
00:07:39,334 --> 00:07:42,162
What if a density is completely flat, from

200
00:07:42,324 --> 00:07:42,965
one to five?

201
00:07:43,387 --> 00:07:44,414
There's no single peak.

202
00:07:45,120 --> 00:07:46,464
How high must it be,

203
00:07:47,007 --> 00:07:48,491
and what does its F look like?

204
00:07:51,195 --> 00:07:52,058
Here are the key notes.

205
00:07:52,461 --> 00:07:54,008
Pause the video if you need more time

206
00:07:54,050 --> 00:07:54,511
to copy them.
